// § caStrengthAndDelayDeclined88 (r11u88) — THE CELL THE PRODUCER DECLINES
// OUTRIGHT, and the transcription of an absence.
//
// THE DECODE is one `else if` in the producer's own parser walk.
// `CompileHelper::compileContinuousAssignment`
// (~/git-repos/Surelog/src/DesignCompile/CompileHelper.cpp:2440-2455) is
// handed the FIRST child of the `Continuous_assign` node and advances ONE
// sibling past whichever of the two optional decorations it finds:
//
//   if (fC->Type(List_of_net_assignments) == VObjectType::paDrive_strength) {
//     … Strength0/Strength1 …
//     List_of_net_assignments = fC->Sibling(List_of_net_assignments);
//   } else if (fC->Type(List_of_net_assignments) == VObjectType::paDelay3) {
//     … delay_expr …
//     List_of_net_assignments = fC->Sibling(List_of_net_assignments);
//   }
//
// The LRM orders them `assign [drive_strength] [delay3] list_of_net_
// assignments ;`, so when BOTH are written the `if` arm takes the strength and
// the ONE advance lands on the `Delay3` node.  `fC->Child(Delay3)` is the
// delay value, whose own children are not a `Net_assignment` shape, so the
// `while (Net_assignment)` loop binds no lvalue and the function returns an
// EMPTY vector: the producer writes NO `cont_assign` for that statement, in
// the definition view and in every elaborated view alike.  Nothing downstream
// can put it back — `UhdmWriter::writeCont_assign`
// (UhdmWriter.cpp:2090) only ever transforms cells that are already in the
// netlist's vector.
//
// MEASURED, not inferred, on golden grids regenerated by the pinned Surelog
// v1.87 (`GRID.pris.r11u88.txt`):
//   z1_bothdrive  `assign (pull1, supply0) #3 c = 32'd10;` in an INTERFACE —
//                 golden lists 0 cells, we list 2 (the def view and the elab
//                 view).  `a7_bothdrive` is the same shape, pass 85's arm.
//   z5_bothmod    the same statement in a MODULE — golden lists 0, we list 2.
//                 The decline is `compileContinuousAssignment`'s and every
//                 home shares it.
//   z6_bothgen    the same in an interface GEN scope and a module GEN scope —
//                 golden 0, we 2.
//   z7_commaboth  `assign (weak1, strong0) #2 p = 32'd1, q = 32'd2;` — BOTH
//                 cells of the comma list are declined (the loop never
//                 starts), while the plain `assign r = …` beside it stands.
//   z2b_delayref  `assign (weak1, strong0) #D c = …;` with a PARAMETER delay
//                 is the same decline; `assign #D c = …;` ALONE is written
//                 (golden carries `vpiDelay: ref_obj D`, and the constant we
//                 write there instead is a SEPARATE residue, untouched here).
//   z3_stronly / z4_dlyonly  the CONTROLS: a strength alone and a delay alone
//                 are both written, and both already read MATCH on every cell.
//
// GOLDEN WRITES NOTHING ON A MISS.  The fix is to stop minting the object, not
// to decorate it: pass 85's drive-field copy landed four more lines on
// `a7_bothdrive`'s ours-only cell (its `ours_only` 42 -> 46, the one rising
// count that pass reported) precisely because the object underneath was one
// golden never writes.
// § caIfaceElabNetDeclAssignListing88 — the ONE predicate that says whether
// the elaborated interface mints a net-declaration-assignment cell for this
// signal, read both by the builder and by the net loop that has to unparent
// the listing typespec when it does.  A declaration carrying a DRIVE STRENGTH
// answers NO: golden writes neither the net nor the cell for it (arm
// `q8_ndastr`, and its module twin `q11_ndastrmod`).
static bool ifaceNdaCellMinted88(const slang::ast::Symbol& sym) {
    if (sym.kind != SymbolKind::Net)
        return false;
    auto* dt = sym.getDeclaredType();
    if (!dt || !dt->getInitializer())
        return false;
    for (auto n = sym.getSyntax(); n; n = n->parent) {
        if (n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::NetDeclaration)
            return n->as<syntax::NetDeclarationSyntax>().strength == nullptr;
        if (n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::InterfaceDeclaration)
            break;
    }
    return true;
}

// ===========================================================================
// § caNetDeclStrengthDropped90 (r11u90) — LAW A: THE STRENGTH-DECORATED NET
// DECLARATION IS NOBODY'S, NET AND CELL ALIKE.  r11u88's R0, closed in the
// two homes pass 87 left standing, and in every view.
//
// THE DECODE is an ARM THAT IS NOT THERE.  The producer's net compiler,
// `CompileHelper::compileNetDeclaration`
// (~/git-repos/Surelog/src/DesignCompile/CompileHelper.cpp:2131-2141), walks
// the declaration's siblings itself:
//
//     nettype = fC->Type(NetType);
//     NodeId net = fC->Sibling(NetTypeOrTrireg_Net);
//     if (fC->Type(net) == VObjectType::paPacked_dimension)
//       List_of_net_decl_assignments = fC->Sibling(net);
//     else
//       List_of_net_decl_assignments = net;
//
// There is NO `paDrive_strength` arm and no `paCharge_strength` arm anywhere
// in the function.  When the declaration is written `wire (strong1, weak0)
// [31:0] w = 32'd12;` that sibling IS the `Drive_strength` node, so
// `List_of_net_decl_assignments` is bound to it; the `paDelay3`/
// `paDelay_control` test below it fails, `fC->Child(Drive_strength)` is the
// strength keyword rather than a `Net_decl_assignment`, and the
// `while (net_decl_assignment)` loop pushes NO `Signal` onto
// `component->getSignals()`.  Nothing downstream can put it back: every net
// UhdmWriter writes comes from that vector, and `NetlistElaboration::
// elabSignal` — the signal walk that mints the net-declaration-assignment
// cells (§ caIfaceElabNetDeclAssignListing88) — walks the same one.  The
// declaration vanishes from both views of every home, net AND cell.
//
// THE PRODUCER SAYS IT IN ITS OWN VOICE.  Arm `u11_strmodport` names the
// dropped net in a modport and Surelog stops with
// `[ERR:CP0311] Undefined net used in modport: "w_str"` — the compiler
// reporting that its own net table has no such entry.
//
// THE GOLDEN GRID (strength shapes x homes x views), every golden
// regenerated by the pinned Surelog v1.87, net listings counted per holder:
//   q8_ndastr      `wire (strong1,weak0) [31:0] w = …;` + `(supply0,supply1)`
//                  in an INTERFACE — golden lists w_plain ALONE in `work@ifc`
//                  and in `work@dut.u_if`; both decorated nets are gone.
//   q11_ndastrmod  the MODULE twin — golden lists `o`,`w_plain` in `work@sub`
//                  and in `work@dut.u_s`; `w_str` is gone from both, and so
//                  is its elaborated net-decl-assign CELL (golden 3 cells,
//                  ours 4).
//   u3_strgenmod / u4_strgenif  the same declaration inside a GENERATE block,
//                  module home and interface home — golden lists
//                  `…u_s.g.w_plain` / `…u_if.g.w_plain` alone, and one cell,
//                  where we list two nets and two cells.
//   u10_strprog    the PROGRAM home — same drop, both views.
//   u5_strread     the decorated net is READ by an outer `assign` — golden
//                  STILL writes no net: a reference does not mint it.
//   u6_strcomma    `wire (strong1,weak0) [31:0] a = 1, b = 2;` — BOTH
//                  declarators go (the loop never starts), while the plain
//                  `wire c = 3;` beside them stands.
//   u7_strdly      a strength AND a delay on the declaration — the strength
//                  arm is the one that is missing, so `w_sd` goes and the
//                  plain `wire [31:0] #3 w_d = …;` beside it stays, delay
//                  and all.
//   u8_strtri      `tri (pull1,pull0)` goes the same way, and the CONTROLS
//                  `supply0 s0; supply1 s1;` — a net TYPE, not a strength —
//                  are kept by golden and by us.
//   u14_strcharge  `trireg (small) t;` — the CHARGE strength is the same
//                  missing arm, and the plain `trireg t_plain;` beside it
//                  stays.
//   u12_strnonansi THE BOUNDARY, and the reason for the port guard below:
//                  `output [31:0] o; wire (strong1,weak0) [31:0] o = 32'd12;`
//                  — golden KEEPS the net (PORT compilation minted it, not
//                  this function) and still declines the CELL.  Net and cell
//                  are two separate answers on this one arm.
//
// GOLDEN WRITES NOTHING ON A MISS: the whole law is the transcription of an
// absence, and nothing here invents a field, an object or a binding.
static bool netDeclStrength90(const slang::ast::Symbol& sym) {
    if (sym.kind != SymbolKind::Net)
        return false;
    if (sym.as<NetSymbol>().isImplicit)
        return false;
    for (auto n = sym.getSyntax(); n; n = n->parent) {
        if (n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::NetDeclaration)
            return n->as<syntax::NetDeclarationSyntax>().strength != nullptr;
        if (n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::ModuleDeclaration ||
            n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::InterfaceDeclaration ||
            n->kind == syntax::SyntaxKind::ProgramDeclaration)
            break;
    }
    return false;
}
// The NET listing's answer.  `isPortNet` is the u12 boundary: a declaration
// that ALSO names a port keeps its net, because the port pass minted it.
// THE TRACE sits OUTSIDE both gates and names EVERY site either law reaches —
// the declined ones and the ones the guards keep — so ONE traced run of ONE
// binary predicts each law's mover set a priori and censuses the residue
// population in the same pass.
static bool strNetDropped90(const slang::ast::Symbol& sym, bool isPortNet,
                            const char* site) {
    const bool str = netDeclStrength90(sym);
    if (cellDbg90() && sym.kind == SymbolKind::Net)
        fprintf(stderr, "R11U90NET site=%s name=%.*s str=%d port=%d drop=%d\n",
                site, (int)sym.name.size(), sym.name.data(), (int)str,
                (int)isPortNet, (int)(str && !isPortNet && !strNetOff90()));
    return str && !isPortNet && !strNetOff90();
}
// The CELL listing's answer — independent of the net's, as `u12_strnonansi`
// proves, and carried on its own switch so either law drops alone.
static bool strCellDropped90(const slang::ast::Symbol& sym, const char* site) {
    const bool str = netDeclStrength90(sym);
    if (cellDbg90() && sym.kind == SymbolKind::Net)
        fprintf(stderr, "R11U90CELL site=%s name=%.*s str=%d drop=%d\n", site,
                (int)sym.name.size(), sym.name.data(), (int)str,
                (int)(str && !strCellOff90()));
    return str && !strCellOff90();
}

// ===========================================================================
// § caIfacePortDeclNetMint93 (r11u93 LAW B) — AN INTERFACE'S NON-ANSI PORT
// DECLARATION MINTS A NET OF ITS OWN, BEFORE EVERY BODY DECLARATION, AND THE
// BODY'S SAME-NAMED DECLARATION KEEPS ITS OWN.  r11u92's R1, closed here in
// both views.
//
// THE DECODE IS ONE MISSING `case`.  `CompileModule::collectModuleObjects_`
// handles a module's non-ANSI HEADER port list at
// `~/git-repos/Surelog/src/DesignCompile/CompileModule.cpp:613`
// (`case VObjectType::paPort:` -> `compilePortDeclaration`, whose `paPort` arm
// pushes one `Signal` per header name onto `component->getPorts()`,
// `CompileHelper.cpp:1737-1757`).  `CompileModule::collectInterfaceObjects_`
// HAS NO `paPort` CASE AT ALL — its switch runs `paPort_declaration`,
// `paAnsi_port_declaration`, `paNet_declaration`, … and never `paPort:`.  So
// when the interface road reaches `output [31:0] o;` and calls
// `setDirectionAndType` (`CompileHelper.cpp:1615-1697`), `module->getPorts()`
// is STILL EMPTY, `found` stays false, and the `found == false` arm
// (`CompileHelper.cpp:1673-1682`) pushes the SAME fresh `Signal` onto
// `getPorts()` **and** `getSignals()`.  The body's `wire [31:0] o = 32'd12;`
// then pushes its OWN `Signal` (`compileNetDeclaration`,
// `CompileHelper.cpp:2184-2206`), and the dedup that closes the DEFINITION
// collect (`CompileModule.cpp:1519-1531`) only appends PORTS MISSING FROM the
// signal list, so it removes neither.  `writeInterface` (`UhdmWriter.cpp:1679`)
// hands `mod->getSignals()` to `writeNets` in that order and every entry
// becomes a net (`UhdmWriter.cpp:889`), so the interface lists the name twice.
// A MODULE never does: its header ports already filled `getPorts()`.
//
// FOUR FACES, four switches, each droppable ALONE:
//   ORDER  the PORT-DECLARATION's, not the header's — `pb16_ifdeclorder`
//          writes `interface ifc (p, o);` above `output o; output p;` and
//          golden lists [o@3:17, p@4:17, o@5:15, p@6:15]: the `Signal`s were
//          created when the DECLARATIONS were walked.  One declaration naming
//          both (`pb17_ifonedecl`) lists them in DECLARATOR order.  The PORT
//          vector obeys the same order, for the same reason — `getPorts()` was
//          filled by the same arm.
//   MINT   the net itself, prepended, `logic_net` whatever the body
//          re-declares it as (`pb11_ifvarredecl`: golden's elaborated view
//          lists the two port-declaration NETS and leaves the body's two
//          `logic` declarations as `vpiVariables`).
//   LOW    the port's `Low_conn` binds the PORT-DECLARATION net and keeps the
//          port-scoped NAMED form: `writeNets` fills `p->Low_conn()` on the
//          FIRST signal of that name (`UhdmWriter.cpp:846-856`) and the second
//          pass finds it non-null and keeps its `Actual_group`
//          (`UhdmWriter.cpp:857-869`) — and `writeInterface` never calls
//          `mapLowConns`, which is exactly what OVERWRITES it on the module
//          road (`UhdmWriter.cpp:1459` vs. its absence at 1681).
//   TYPE   a mint whose body declaration the STRENGTH law erased carries NO
//          `vpiNetType`: the port `Signal` is typed by
//          `compileNetDeclaration`'s `portRef->setType(fC->Type(NetType))` loop
//          (`CompileHelper.cpp:2157-2163`), and the declaration that loop never
//          reached is the one § caNetDeclStrengthDropped90 removed.  `n3`
//          golden: `o` (strength) prints `vpiName`/`vpiFullName` and nothing
//          else, `p` (plain `wire`) beside it prints `vpiNetType:1`.
//
// THE GRID (goldens regenerated by the pinned Surelog v1.87; the interface's
// own `vpiNet`, def view `work@ifc` and elab view `work@dut.u_if` ALIKE):
//   n4_nonansi_plain_if  both plain     [o@5:17, p@6:17, o@7:15, p@8:15]
//   n3_strnonansi_if     strength on o  [o@3:17, p@4:17, p@6:15] — one `o`
//   pb14_ifbothstr       both strength  [o@3:17, p@4:17]
//   pb3_ifnoredecl       no body `o`    [o@3:17, p@4:17, p@5:15]
//   pb4_ifrevorder       body reversed  [o@4:17, p@5:17, p@6:15, o@7:15]
//   pb5_ifinput          an INPUT port  same shape — not a direction
//   pb7_iftwoports       3 ports + mid  [o,p,r decls][o, mid, p, r body]
//   pb15_ifnodim         no packed dim  same shape
//   pb9_ifgen / pb8_ifmodport  a generate block / a modport beside: unchanged
//   pb10_ifnetuse        the net READ by a body assign: unchanged
//   pb12_ifstrnonport    a strength net that is NOT a port: still dropped
//   pb19_modportview     a MODPORT PORT VIEW lists NO nets at all (`vpiNet`
//                        empty on `work@dut.u_s.m`): the mint is a HOME-view
//                        object.  THE CONTROL the face needed.
//   pb13_ifnoansiplainnouse / pb6_ifansi  THE CONTROLS: no body declarations
//                        at all, and the ANSI header — `cmp rc=0` on the
//                        pristine binary and unmoved here.
//   pb18_ifnodecl        a header port with NO port declaration: the pinned
//                        SURELOG REJECTS it (`golden_rc=4`), so the shape
//                        where `getPorts()` would stay empty is unreachable.
//
// GOLDEN WRITES NOTHING ON A MISS: the mint fires ONLY where a
// `PortDeclarationSyntax` declarator names a port of a NON-ANSI INTERFACE
// header, which is precisely where Surelog's `found == false` arm runs.
static bool ifPortMintOff93() {
    static const bool v = envSet("R11U93_IFPORTMINT_OFF") ||
                          envSet("R11U93_OFF");
    return v;
}
