// § caIfacePortDeclNetMint93 face SRCORD (v11u93 VERIFIER fix) — the
// PORT-DECLARATION nets are NOT a block in front of the body's: the producer
// pushes one `Signal` per declaration AS THE COLLECT WALK REACHES IT
// (`CompileHelper.cpp:1673-1682` for a port declaration,
// `CompileHelper.cpp:2184-2206` for a net declaration, both driven by
// `collectInterfaceObjects_`'s single source-order walk), and `writeInterface`
// hands that vector to `writeNets` unchanged (`UhdmWriter.cpp:1679`).  So the
// two groups INTERLEAVE BY SOURCE ORDER, which only looks like a prepend when
// every port declaration precedes every body declaration — true of every arm
// in the r11u93 grid, false as soon as a body net is written first:
//   v1_ifnetbeforeport  `wire mid;` ABOVE `output o; output p;`
//       golden  [mid@3:15, o@4:17, p@5:17, o@6:15, p@7:15]
//       prepend [o@4:17, p@5:17, mid@3:15, o@6:15, p@7:15]   <- 23 cmp lines
//   v10_ifportmid       `wire mid;` BETWEEN the two port declarations
//       golden  [o@3:17, mid@4:15, p@5:17, o@6:15, p@7:15]
//       prepend [o@3:17, p@5:17, mid@4:15, o@6:15, p@7:15]   <- 23 cmp lines
// Merging the mints into the base listing's leading (location-sorted) run by
// source location reproduces golden on both, and is a NO-OP on every arm the
// prepend already got right.
static bool ifPortSrcOrdOff93() {
    static const bool v = envSet("R11U93_IFPORTSRCORD_OFF") ||
                          envSet("R11U93_OFF");
    return v;
}
// § caIfacePortDeclNetMint93 face TYPE (v11u93 VERIFIER widening) — the mint
// carries a net type ONLY where a BODY NET DECLARATION was walked AFTER the
// port declaration.  `compileNetDeclaration` types the port Signal from the
// NET DECLARATION's side (`CompileHelper.cpp:2158-2163`: it scans
// `component->getPorts()` for the name and calls `port->setType(...)` right
// there), so a net declaration the walk reaches BEFORE the port declaration
// finds no port to type, exactly as the strength-erased declaration the
// § caNetDeclStrengthDropped90 drop removed finds none.  THREE readings of
// the same rule, all measured on v1.87 goldens:
//   pb13_ifnoansiplainnouse  no body declaration at all   -> NO vpiNetType
//   pb3_ifnoredecl           `o` undeclared, `p` declared -> o NONE, p 1
//   n3_strnonansi_if         `o` strength-erased          -> o NONE, p 1
//   v15_ifdeclafterbody      `wire o;` ABOVE `output o;`  -> NO vpiNetType
// The first three the base and the r11u93 gate already agree on; the fourth
// is the one the strength-only gate wrote `vpiNetType:1` into (15 cmp lines),
// a field golden does not have on that object.
static bool mintUntyped93(const Symbol& sym, slang::SourceLocation portDeclLoc) {
    if (netDeclStrength90(sym))
        return true;
    return hasBodyDecl(sym) && portDeclLoc != SourceLocation::NoLocation &&
           sym.location < portDeclLoc;
}
